{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders","id":846804,"title":"A take on Elders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-13T17:02:37-07:00","id":846804,"title":"A take on Elders","content":"So, my most recent flight of fancy was a take on Vampiric Elders.<br /> <br /> My basic thought process was that the idea of Elder Devotions just doesn't sit right with me as the main benefit Elders get, but at the same time, just copying 6+ dot disciplines from cWoD or 1st edition allusions also didn't feel right. So, I decided on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OyVs-12emmgTK6XSu6dgmACqv7B8TpZuJv2z-9A7yxw/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Elder Transmutations</a>. What they are is essentially new template abilities, sort of like Bloodline Gifts, but more powerful, and unique to a given Elder rather than an entire bloodline.<br /> <br /> By default, it's simply something elders (BP 6+ Kindred) can purchase, a new option, rather than a new full template (like Archmages), but for the fun of it, I also included a sidebar on the last page for a potential way to handle Elders as a Tier 4 template, incorporating Transmutations as part of it, though I'm open for suggestions to give them a more innately cosmological scale.<br /> <br /> There's a fairly decent smattering of example Transmutations there, and if people like the idea I might go ahead and think up some more. Let me know what you all think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-14-2016, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T18:16:22-07:00","id":846839,"title":"","content":"Dang. You really gave two options that are equally interesting in their own right. I just <i>might</i> incorporate this somehow. One thing, though. Instead of calling them Elder Transmutations, why not take the term &quot;Blood Secrets&quot;, which was used in one of the 1E supplements.<br /> <br /> Either way, I find myself asking another question. What happens to those powers if an Elder is reduced in Blood Potency? Can he still use them? Or are they rendered inert until he becomes powerful, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T18:44:18-07:00","id":846857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=846839#post846839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang. You really gave two options that are equally interesting in their own right. I just <i>might</i> incorporate this somehow. One thing, though. Instead of calling them Elder Transmutations, why not take the term &quot;Blood Secrets&quot;, which was used in one of the 1E supplements.<br /> <br /> Either way, I find myself asking another question. What happens to those powers if an Elder is reduced in Blood Potency? Can he still use them? Or are they rendered inert until he becomes powerful, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I had forgotten about those. The only issue there is those that are aware of Blood Secrets might confuse them for the more universally accessible ones.<br /> <br /> As for the question, I have that covered in there; you retain all Transmutations until your Blood Potency drops to 5 or less, at which point you can't use them, though they never leave your sheet (so you'll get them back when you raise your BP back up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T18:46:08-07:00","id":846859,"title":"","content":"I... Really like this homebrew. And I don't often like homebrew... Really I generally wouldn't look twice at most of it or even consider it for my games. But this seemed to fit into some of the things I was working on in my old Methuselah project that I abandoned. I like that there was a lot of flexibility to the permanency abilities rather than focusing on individual discipline usage.<br /> <br /> Like I would seriously like them to tap you for the Thousand Years of Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 03-13-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T19:08:52-07:00","id":846872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=846859#post846859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... Really like this homebrew. And I don't often like homebrew... Really I generally wouldn't look twice at most of it or even consider it for my games. But this seemed to fit into some of the things I was working on in my old Methuselah project that I abandoned. I like that there was a lot of flexibility to the permanency abilities rather than focusing on individual discipline usage.<br /> <br /> Like I would seriously like them to tap you for the Thousand Years of Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had actually seen that before and liked it, but noticed it was never finished. I admittedly did tap a couple things I saw there in the optional elder template I put at the end; namely the ability to return from many forms of final death and the lack of blood potency lowering in torpor, though I simplified them since it wasn't the main focus of the document.<br /> <br /> Regardless, thanks for the praise!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T19:26:47-07:00","id":846876,"title":"","content":"Could you clarify what you mean by truly permanent effects in Elder Will? Do you mean Disciplines effected by Permanency or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T19:28:56-07:00","id":846877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=846876#post846876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you clarify what you mean by truly permanent effects in Elder Will? Do you mean Disciplines effected by Permanency or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that disciplines benefiting from that dice pool don't automatically have the +4 bonus that Elder Transmutations gain in general (since they're effectively permanent), they need to actually last for an indefinite duration. In the case of Disciplines affected by Permanency, they'd get the +4 bonus, yes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Blatantly pointed that out and reworded it a little bit to make it clear, on the document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-13-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:10:22-07:00","id":846890,"title":"","content":"So age doesn't come into play? The word elder is being used a lot but the only across-the-board prerequisite seems to be Blood Potency 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:18:53-07:00","id":846893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=846890#post846890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So age doesn't come into play? The word elder is being used a lot but the only across-the-board prerequisite seems to be Blood Potency 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as a hard prerequisite, no. There's other ways to raise Blood Potency, but in general, the books have always seemed to call BP 6+ Vamps elders regardless of age, and I didn't see any need to put a specific age as a requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:51:30-07:00","id":846906,"title":"","content":"Any chance for some healing enhancement transmutation example? Either for enhanced vitae healing or agg healing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:39:23-07:00","id":846927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=846906#post846906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance for some healing enhancement transmutation example? Either for enhanced vitae healing or agg healing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Done. See Tireless Regeneration and Rote Healing at BP 6 and 7, respectively. Debating if I want to switch those requirements around or not.<br /> <br /> Also, should alphabetize these within a given BP range...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Changed Rote Healing a bit to make it a bit more obviously a BP7 power, giving them a couple benefits in addition to the doubled healing rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-14-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T01:31:08-07:00","id":846974,"title":"","content":"Say, if I were to reskin the Revivifying Feeding hack from Armory Reloaded as an Elder Transmutation/Blood Secret, would Blood Potency 6 be a good requirement for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T02:08:31-07:00","id":846978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=846974#post846974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, if I were to reskin the Revivifying Feeding hack from Armory Reloaded as an Elder Transmutation/Blood Secret, would Blood Potency 6 be a good requirement for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Blood Potency 6 would be fine for that, yeah, as while it does provide additional healing, it's limited to lethal damage at most, and requires feeding specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:01:00-07:00","id":847015,"title":"","content":"One thing to note: you seem to be under the impression that vampires need two days to heal an aggravated wound. That's no longer the case in second edition. They only need one now. Also the FAQ indicates that with sufficient vitae they can heal multiple aggravated in a single day. The only requirement is that they are asleep when they do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:31:01-07:00","id":847132,"title":"","content":"Ooh, this is a wonderfully horrifying concept. I do second the idea of that there should be something to catalyze the change from a regular Blood Potency 6+ Kindred to an Elder, which here seem more similar to V:tM Methuselahs and Antediluvians than anything else, if only for the fact that there's a pretty dramatic shift from the regular Vampire template.<br /> <br /> That being said, Permanence, Ever-Raised Hackles, and Immutable Power are probably my favourite Elder Transmutations. It really projects the image of an Elder as some kind of indomitable, hyper-aware creature that's beyond the normal limits of the Kindred condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:46:53-07:00","id":847146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847132#post847132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, this is a wonderfully horrifying concept. I do second the idea of that there should be something to catalyze the change from a regular Blood Potency 6+ Kindred to an Elder, which here seem more similar to V:tM Methuselahs and Antediluvians than anything else, if only for the fact that there's a pretty dramatic shift from the regular Vampire template.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tend to agree. The Zagreus previews (both the methulelah addon from rose, and immortal sinners) seemed to indicate that SOMETHING dramatic should be required for the change other than just Blood potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:40:48-07:00","id":847241,"title":"","content":"Mmrrrr...... *glances through* Well, not bad, but one thing springs instantly to mind. I honestly think you're trying to equate vampire elders to archmages or Gentry here. Elders are equivalent to Master mages or the royalty of Changeling Courts. The Methusalah, vampires who surpass elders, are the ones who adapt new templates like Archmages and True Fae. Of course you'll be disappointed if you think that elder devotions are supposed to be the equivalent of archmastery. They're not.<br /> <br /> Not to say there's not demand for a Methusalah power set and template. There is. Some people get great use out of the Archmage book, though I personally never had the need for it. But you're misidentifying what being an elder means.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Now, on to the actual abilities... honeslty, if this is supposed to be the equivalent of a vampire evolution, you are being far too tame. The overwhelming majority of these are reporducable as devotions, Coils, or merits; Celeritous Power has a low level equivalent in Hint of Fear, just expanded to other Disciplines, which other low-level Devotions could do as well. Or, like Permanency, some of these Transmutations don't really do anything of note. I'm sorry, but if your goal was to have advanced abilities for vampires, reproducing things that neonates could have access to is far too tame. <br /> <br /> There is only one worthwhile ability - the one that gives Clash of Wills rote quality, and I personally find the idea of switching to attributes to be a deliberate break from and added complexity to the rules for no reason other than more dice to be distasteful. While it does offset the powercreep of other gamelines casually gaining rote quality, its pretty much only useful on crossover; you're already going to win a Clash of Wills by virtue of simply having higher BP. <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, on to the template. <br /> - Free transmutation. Bleh. <br /> - no loss of BP in torpor. Pretty standard according to legends of the Methusalah. I wouldn' texpect such a template without at least this much.<br /> - Everything is now affinity cost in terms of disciplines. Just... why? Feels like you're trying to eliminate clan here. No reason for it; even Archmages don't eliminate Path affinities.<br /> - Cannot be diablarized except by another Methusalah. Again, why? Feels more like power creep than something that involves story. Power hungry vampire who wants to devour the soul of an ancient is a classic plot hook, and this gets in the way. If you've already reached the point where you could theoretically be diablarized? You're as good as dead. I fail to see the point of even having this as a thing.<br /> - No need to spend willpower to Lash Out. Okay, that's pretty nice effect, and thematic.<br /> - The anti-Auspex 5 ability. Sounds like you have a beef with Auspex that you wanted to plug, not something worth noting about ancient vampires.<br /> - Devotion creation - this is actually a possibility for neonates developing Devotions as it is. This does nothing.<br /> - Hard to kill. Part of the whole &quot;can only be killed by another ancient diablarizing&quot; theme running through the place, which I think gets in the way of stories more than not. I also think that Final Death by fire or sunlight shouldn't be excluded. YMMV. <br /> <br /> So, other than the torpor bits, costless Lashing Out, and &quot;can only be killed by acients diablarizing each other&quot; parts, I think the majority is rather pointless, reproducing low level things, or flat out unthematic. It doesn't even touch on Banes or the like, something I imagine would be rather critical for ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:01:02-07:00","id":847249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847015#post847015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to note: you seem to be under the impression that vampires need two days to heal an aggravated wound. That's no longer the case in second edition. They only need one now. Also the FAQ indicates that with sufficient vitae they can heal multiple aggravated in a single day. The only requirement is that they are asleep when they do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're right, I'll go ahead and tweak the appropriate Transmutations. I've been playing 1e on a chat lately, so those rules keep creeping into my head. Maybe I'll switch it so they only need 2 Vitae per aggravated wound with Rote Healing since the speed isn't an issue anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847146#post847146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I tend to agree. The Zagreus previews (both the methulelah addon from rose, and immortal sinners) seemed to indicate that SOMETHING dramatic should be required for the change other than just Blood potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did mention in the elder template at the bottom that some story justification is likely needed, but didn't really pre-define something if you're only using the Transmutations themselves. That is, if there's no real template for them, I figure it's up to the Storyteller when a vampire can take those since it's a purely story focus anyway. I'll maybe add a note that in some chronicles developing elder transmutations might require some sort of transformation of its own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847241#post847241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmrrrr...... *glances through* Well, not bad, but one thing springs instantly to mind. I honestly think you're trying to equate vampire elders to archmages or Gentry here. Elders are equivalent to Master mages or the royalty of Changeling Courts. The Methusalah, vampires who surpass elders, are the ones who adapt new templates like Archmages and True Fae. Of course you'll be disappointed if you think that elder devotions are supposed to be the equivalent of archmastery. They're not.<br /> <br /> Not to say there's not demand for a Methusalah power set and template. There is. Some people get great use out of the Archmage book, though I personally never had the need for it. But you're misidentifying what being an elder means.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted, the Elder template itself is more or less a quick and dirty patch to grant some benefits if you want something at a higher level of play. But the Elder Transmutation rules themselves don't really do that, they just give you some more powerful options; my goal if you're JUST using them is to have something a step above other Kindred but not really 4th tier play on its own. It's a little in between (Which, if everyone's playing an elder, isn't likely an issue).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, for what it's worth, I think the only time Methuselah as a word is actually used in 2e is as a suggested Experience level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, on to the actual abilities... honeslty, if this is supposed to be the equivalent of a vampire evolution, you are being far too tame. The overwhelming majority of these are reporducable as devotions, Coils, or merits; Celeritous Power has a low level equivalent in Hint of Fear, just expanded to other Disciplines, which other low-level Devotions could do as well. Or, like Permanency, some of these Transmutations don't really do anything of note. I'm sorry, but if your goal was to have advanced abilities for vampires, reproducing things that neonates could have access to is far too tame.<br /> <br /> There is only one worthwhile ability - the one that gives Clash of Wills rote quality, and I personally find the idea of switching to attributes to be a deliberate break from and added complexity to the rules for no reason other than more dice to be distasteful. While it does offset the powercreep of other gamelines casually gaining rote quality, its pretty much only useful on crossover; you're already going to win a Clash of Wills by virtue of simply having higher BP. </div> </div> </div>Hmm. You may be right, about being too tame, with some of them. I do agree some could be reproduced, at least for the ones at BP 6-7. I dunno, what do other people think about that?<br /> <br /> As for the Clash of Wills benefit, there's a lot of powers in games that simply give you more dice. And as for rote quality being unneeded, I disagree. Even ignoring other gamelines, if you don't have this, an Elder with, say, 2 dots in a Discipline and a BP of 6 versus a neonate of BP2 but with 4 dots, you're at 8 dice vs 6 dice there. This would then give that elder, who likely has an attribute of at least 5 in there, to have a dice pool of 11 rote vs 6, which is a bit more one sided, and of course needs a transmutation to get them there. Also, I don't see how 'highest attribute' is very complex. If anything, it makes it simpler; once you take this, you can note down your clash of wills dice pool without checking which power rating you're using each time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, on to the template.<br /> - Free transmutation. Bleh.<br /> - no loss of BP in torpor. Pretty standard according to legends of the Methusalah. I wouldn' texpect such a template without at least this much.<br /> - Everything is now affinity cost in terms of disciplines. Just... why? Feels like you're trying to eliminate clan here. No reason for it; even Archmages don't eliminate Path affinities.<br /> - Cannot be diablarized except by another Methusalah. Again, why? Feels more like power creep than something that involves story. Power hungry vampire who wants to devour the soul of an ancient is a classic plot hook, and this gets in the way. If you've already reached the point where you could theoretically be diablarized? You're as good as dead. I fail to see the point of even having this as a thing.<br /> - No need to spend willpower to Lash Out. Okay, that's pretty nice effect, and thematic.<br /> - The anti-Auspex 5 ability. Sounds like you have a beef with Auspex that you wanted to plug, not something worth noting about ancient vampires.<br /> - Devotion creation - this is actually a possibility for neonates developing Devotions as it is. This does nothing.<br /> - Hard to kill. Part of the whole &quot;can only be killed by another ancient diablarizing&quot; theme running through the place, which I think gets in the way of stories more than not. I also think that Final Death by fire or sunlight shouldn't be excluded. YMMV.<br /> <br /> So, other than the torpor bits, costless Lashing Out, and &quot;can only be killed by acients diablarizing each other&quot; parts, I think the majority is rather pointless, reproducing low level things, or flat out unthematic. It doesn't even touch on Banes or the like, something I imagine would be rather critical for ancients. </div> </div> </div>Archmages DO remove the differing costs for affinities, I literally took that directly from Imperial Mysteries. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Archmages lack Ruling, Common or Inferior Arcana, but<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">learn all Arcana at (new dots x 6) experience</span></span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> You may be right about the Diablerie point, I hadn't considered that I'd be removing a major plot hook. I borrowed that from Imperial Mysteries too. I'll change it so only DIablerie in general can do it, and maybe note that a failure causes problems for the aggressor. An instant vinculum or something, since they can then revive as normal.<br /> <br /> That's not anti auspex 5, it makes projection and possession type abilities better for the Elder. I find it silly that a projecting Elder could be possessed by a piddling low rank spirit and then have difficulty getting back into their body, you know?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by Devotion creation. Is there something I missed that grants beats back?<br /> <br /> I DIDN'T exclude final death by fire and sunlight. They're one of the noted ways you CAN kill them. You just need to fully do it that way (no filling to agg with rolled over baseball bat damage then burning their hand with a lighter).<br /> <br /> As for banes, I explicitly left that out, as that seems like something to be covered by Mysteries of the Dragon. (Though, you'll note there's a Transmutation to let any elder learn one, if they want to go that route)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-14-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:55:34-07:00","id":847290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847249#post847249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also, for what it's worth, I think the only time Methuselah as a word is actually used in 2e is as a suggested Experience level.</div> </div> </div> </div> Methusaelah is described in length in other books, which are listed as inspirational material in the front of 2e. So, while there's not quite a direct mention, its definitely implied as part of the background that 2e core was meant to update to. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . I do agree some could be reproduced, at least for the ones at BP 6-7. </div> </div> </div> Up through 9 at least. The one about true immortality and clash of wills are the only ones that I couldn't see reproduced elsewhere, or easily made into a devotion, since they're just fiddling with existing powers. Hells, your level 9 power is a reproduction of a current devotion, just for any power instead of just Nightmare. The overwhelming majority already exist in some other form in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Clash of Wills benefit, there's a lot of powers in games that simply give you more dice. </div> </div> </div> The problem is that you are taking a system meant to work on evoking certain themes, and changing what it means at a fundamental level merely for the sake of extra dice. You want extra dice, fine. The problem I have is that there are more elegant ways of doing it that retain the feel and purpose of the mechanics. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Archmages DO remove the differing costs for affinities, I literally took that directly from Imperial Mysteries. </div> </div> </div> Fair enough, I misremembered. However, I maintain that, while it may be appropriate for Mage, it is not appropriate for Vampire with its emphasis on bloodlines and family and sympathetic connections. <br /> <br /> In Mage, I can see where you grow beyond the need for Oracle-established Watchtowers and develop your own styematic connection to the Supernal. In Vampire, however? At best, you're establishing your own Clan, which should develop its own affinities, since they will be passed down to your childer. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I borrowed that from Imperial Mysteries too. I'll change it so only DIablerie in general can do it, and maybe note that a failure causes problems for the aggressor. An instant vinculum or something, since they can then revive as normal. </div> </div> </div> Vampire isn't Mage. The two evoke different methods and themes and story needs. Now, if you want to evoke the whole idea of being super-undead to the point that almost nothing short of soul destruction can end you, that'd be one thing. But it feels like you're just copying Mage stuff without an eye towards Vampire themes. And I really, really have to object to that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it silly that a projecting Elder could be possessed by a piddling low rank spirit and then have difficulty getting back into their body, you know? </div> </div> </div> No, I don't know, considering that its not mentioned at all in 2e. That's a 1e-ism. <br /> <br /> Neither Possession nor Twilight Projection send your soul out and leave your body open for possession. You just extend your senses away from your body. If a spirit or ghost or whatever wants a vampire body, they have to take it over in the same way it would try to take over a fully awake vampire. In the case of an ephemeral entity, they need to arrange things so that the vampire body has an Open Condition, as per normal rules. In the case of a strix, that means beating the body into torpor. Given that your senses can't detect what is happening to your body, it could be an issue by granting the entity the time to arrange said conditions. But there is nothing that lets something walk in and take over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what you mean by Devotion creation. Is there something I missed that grants beats back? </div> </div> </div> The method of creating Devotions is the same, and you can get a Condition for beats on the matter. <br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but is this something else that you took from Imperial Mysteries? Learning new magic granting Arcane EXP equivalents is understandable for a mage. For a vampire? We have Blood Beats for an equivalent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I DIDN'T exclude final death by fire and sunlight. They're one of the noted ways you CAN kill them. You just need to fully do it that way (no filling to agg with rolled over baseball bat damage then burning their hand with a lighter). </div> </div> </div> Misunderstood that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for banes, I explicitly left that out, as that seems like something to be covered by Mysteries of the Dragon. (Though, you'll note there's a Transmutation to let any elder learn one, if they want to go that route) </div> </div> </div> I did note the Transmuation, but consider that Transmutation redundant - any ancient worth their salt can merely learn a power through stealing it via Disciplines. <br /> <br /> However, I feel compelled to point out that &quot;banes are the domain of Coils&quot; is a mistaken impression from 1e. Coils no longer deal exclusively with vampire weaknesses. Dealing with Banes could be done through any power, be it Theban, Cruac, Coil, Oath, Law, or something more exotic like unique magics, bloodlines or a deal with a strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:14:04-07:00","id":847296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847290#post847290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Methusaelah is described in length in other books, which are listed as inspirational material in the front of 2e. So, while there's not quite a direct mention, its definitely implied as part of the background that 2e core was meant to update to.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough, my main point there was simply that I don't see this as necesarrily needing to be labeled Methuselahs to have this level of power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Up through 9 at least. The one about true immortality and clash of wills are the only ones that I couldn't see reproduced elsewhere, or easily made into a devotion, since they're just fiddling with existing powers. Hells, your level 9 power is a reproduction of a current devotion, just for any power instead of just Nightmare. The overwhelming majority already exist in some other form in the game. </div> </div> </div>You'd need a devotion for every single power you had, which would be a hefty sum of Experience and time to develop, and a new one would be needed for each one. I think you're downplaying just how powerful it being reflexive for everything really is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that you are taking a system meant to work on evoking certain themes, and changing what it means at a fundamental level merely for the sake of extra dice. You want extra dice, fine. The problem I have is that there are more elegant ways of doing it that retain the feel and purpose of the mechanics. </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, I think the thematic of gaining the same control over their disciplines that they do over their more innate abilities as an elder (the Transmutations) is very thematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fair enough, I misremembered. However, I maintain that, while it may be appropriate for Mage, it is not appropriate for Vampire with its emphasis on bloodlines and family and sympathetic connections.<br /> <br /> In Mage, I can see where you grow beyond the need for Oracle-established Watchtowers and develop your own styematic connection to the Supernal. In Vampire, however? At best, you're establishing your own Clan, which should develop its own affinities, since they will be passed down to your childer.<br /> <br /> Vampire isn't Mage. The two evoke different methods and themes and story needs. Now, if you want to evoke the whole idea of being super-undead to the point that almost nothing short of soul destruction can end you, that'd be one thing. But it feels like you're just copying Mage stuff without an eye towards Vampire themes. And I really, really have to object to that. </div> </div> </div>Borrowing a couple of template abilities doesn't mean I'm making vampire into mage. They're things I saw as high tier abilities. And it DOES make sense to me for an elder to grow past their clan affinities. Just because they might pass them down to lesser kindred doesn't mean they have to rely on the power of their lineage instead of what they themself have developed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I don't know, considering that its not mentioned at all in 2e. That's a 1e-ism.<br /> <br /> Neither Possession nor Twilight Projection send your soul out and leave your body open for possession. You just extend your senses away from your body. If a spirit or ghost or whatever wants a vampire body, they have to take it over in the same way it would try to take over a fully awake vampire. In the case of an ephemeral entity, they need to arrange things so that the vampire body has an Open Condition, as per normal rules. In the case of a strix, that means beating the body into torpor. Given that your senses can't detect what is happening to your body, it could be an issue by granting the entity the time to arrange said conditions. But there is nothing that lets something walk in and take over. </div> </div> </div>Auspex 5 mentions strange magics could prevent it, and implies Strix possession could. Don't have the book open to Dominate's possession right now, but I imagine similar things could stop one from returning in that case too. And I don't think an Elder should be displaced as easily as a neonate there; he gets a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The method of creating Devotions is the same, and you can get a Condition for beats on the matter.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but is this something else that you took from Imperial Mysteries? Learning new magic granting Arcane EXP equivalents is understandable for a mage. For a vampire? We have Blood Beats for an equivalent. </div> </div> </div>No, that's something I just decided made sense; it's easier for elders to toy with the way their powers work. In either case, it'd be on top of anything gained from conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did note the Transmuation, but consider that Transmutation redundant - any ancient worth their salt can merely learn a power through stealing it via Disciplines.<br /> <br /> However, I feel compelled to point out that &quot;banes are the domain of Coils&quot; is a mistaken impression from 1e. Coils no longer deal exclusively with vampire weaknesses. Dealing with Banes could be done through any power, be it Theban, Cruac, Coil, Oath, Law, or something more exotic like unique magics, bloodlines or a deal with a strix. </div> </div> </div>It's not redundant, considering there's not always an option to find ways to gain those powers otherwise. And I know Coils don't exclusively deal with banes, but they do tend to deal with transcending the vampiric condition, and I don't want to overlap too much. THAT would be redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-14-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:19:55-07:00","id":847468,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, I've gone ahead and boosted the power of some of the Transmutations, some a tiny bit, and some a fair bit more. Of note, Permanency and Immutable Power got a big boost, now only requiring a night long duration or a turn-long duration (essentially anything non-instantaneous), respectively.<br /> <br /> Going to also work on adding a few new ones since I'm mostly getting positive feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:28:31-07:00","id":847474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders#post846804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my most recent flight of fancy was a take on Vampiric Elders.<br /> <br /> My basic thought process was that the idea of Elder Devotions just doesn't sit right with me as the main benefit Elders get, but at the same time, just copying 6+ dot disciplines from cWoD or 1st edition allusions also didn't feel right. So, I decided on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OyVs-12emmgTK6XSu6dgmACqv7B8TpZuJv2z-9A7yxw/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Elder Transmutations</a>. What they are is essentially new template abilities, sort of like Bloodline Gifts, but more powerful, and unique to a given Elder rather than an entire bloodline.<br /> <br /> By default, it's simply something elders (BP 6+ Kindred) can purchase, a new option, rather than a new full template (like Archmages), but for the fun of it, I also included a sidebar on the last page for a potential way to handle Elders as a Tier 4 template, incorporating Transmutations as part of it, though I'm open for suggestions to give them a more innately cosmological scale.<br /> <br /> There's a fairly decent smattering of example Transmutations there, and if people like the idea I might go ahead and think up some more. Let me know what you all think!</div> </div> </div> </div>While Elder devotions don't bother me, I find this interesting. When you say 4 xp is that old or new(20 beats)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:31:09-07:00","id":847476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847474#post847474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Elder devotions don't bother me, I find this interesting. When you say 4 xp is that old or new(20 beats)?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, elder devotions don't bother me, it just doesn't quite seem to fulfill what I think of as elder capabilities, at least on their own.<br /> <br /> And it's 4 Experiences, this is 2e stuff of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:16:27-07:00","id":847493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847476#post847476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be clear, elder devotions don't bother me, it just doesn't quite seem to fulfill what I think of as elder capabilities, at least on their own.<br /> <br /> And it's 4 Experiences, this is 2e stuff of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like enhanced servant. Anything xtra for ghouled families?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:17:49-07:00","id":847496,"title":"","content":"Define Rote Quality please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:19:45-07:00","id":847498,"title":"","content":"Ghoul families don't have full mechanics yet, they're sort of vague in the benefits they might have, so I don't want to toy with special addons for them. They would benefit the same as any other ghoul, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:36:06-07:00","id":847505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847498#post847498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghoul families don't have full mechanics yet, they're sort of vague in the benefits they might have, so I don't want to toy with special addons for them. They would benefit the same as any other ghoul, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Nods*. May be for the best. Until that gets ironed out. Though Rose did say the get the ability to detect kindred.<br /> <br /> In general what is &quot;Rote Quality&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:37:02-07:00","id":847507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847505#post847505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Nods*. May be for the best. Until that gets ironed out. Though Rose did say the get the ability to detect kindred.<br /> <br /> In general what is &quot;Rote Quality&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's listed in all the cores, it's a dice trick like 9 again or 8 again; it rerolls failed dice one time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T02:25:37-07:00","id":847586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847476#post847476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be clear, elder devotions don't bother me, it just doesn't quite seem to fulfill what I think of as elder capabilities, at least on their own.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm still not sure where you're getting this. One of your transmutations <i>is </i>a devotion, from the 1e Carthians book. So it seems the problem is not that elder devotions don't fulfil the cababilities you want, but rather that you're underselling what elder devotions are capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T02:59:42-07:00","id":847593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847586#post847586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I'm still not sure where you're getting this. One of your transmutations <i>is </i>a devotion, from the 1e Carthians book. So it seemseems the problem is not tht elder devotions don't fulfil the cababilities you want, but rather that you're underselling what elder devotions are capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which devotion is that? Regardless, I guess the main thing is I dislike the notion of elders relying so fully on just recombining their disciplines in new ways. Sure that should be an option, but I wanted to provide something else that works a little differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T03:24:55-07:00","id":847599,"title":"","content":"Regeneration, page 198. Requires protean 4 and resilience 4, so under the new experience system is would even cost 4 experiences,making it completely identical to Tireless Regeneration aside from the prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T04:51:43-07:00","id":847616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847593#post847593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which devotion is that? Regardless, I guess the main thing is I dislike the notion of elders relying so fully on just recombining their disciplines in new ways. Sure that should be an option, but I wanted to provide something else that works a little differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but what's the point of making up a completely new system when the old one can do the job?<br /> <br /> Let's see, going over your document seeing what devotions these could be:<br /> Apex's Aura - Dominate, Nightmare or Majesty devotion depending on which Bestial Aspect you want to enhance<br /> Elder Will - Vigor, Auspex devotion.<br /> Enhanced Servant - Dominate with some Resilience. Buffing your underlings is already possible with Dominate devotions so this is rather an easy one<br /> Ever-Raised Hackles - Auspex, devotion, costing some vitae each month or so to keep it running permanently.<br /> Innate Sorcery - uh, first half of this thing is not worthwhile having at all. Just let the elders learn those things on their own. Second part could be a devotion based on the Sorcery and Vigor.<br /> Permanency - Resilience, of course... the description practically begs for this as it uses &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">resiliency </span></span>&quot; in it.<br /> Sympathetic Defense - again a fairly simple devotion, based on Auspex to detect these things, and on whatever power we want to be able to shoot back.<br /> Tireless regeneration - already covered by Elfive.<br /> Evolved Form - description is completely outdated. Nowadays elders are fast learners, not slow learners. But in any case, Protean is the one for this.<br /> Fleeting Flesh - Protean and Resilience<br /> Immutable Power - Resilience again,.<br /> Improved Diablerie - Seems like this could just as well be a merit, but if going the devotion route it could be Auspex.<br /> Rote Healing - Resilience.<br /> Supernatural Negation - More Resilience<br /> Perfected Diablerie - just no.<br /> Soul Bond - screams Dominate all over the thing.<br /> Celeritious Power - Do I even need to say it or will pointing at it's name be enough?<br /> <br /> <br /> Really, when I started this list, I thought it's gonna be hard one. But for the most part, these powers fit in devotions so <b>neatly, </b>that I was quite surprised.<br /> So anyways, this does not work a little differently. It's just superficial differences at most, as we get to call these Devotions a different name with a little different pricing scheme.<br /> <br /> And that can be achieved much more easily, by providing a small &quot;elder&quot; template, which allows an Elder to use some Devotions much more cheaply than their counterparts can, giving all and more to the possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 03-15-2016, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T05:48:14-07:00","id":847633,"title":"","content":"Celeritious Power would at least be a bunch of devotions, not just one. <i>That</i> I can see counting as an Elder Upgrade Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T06:06:22-07:00","id":847642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847633#post847633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celeritious Power would at least be a bunch of devotions, not just one. <i>That</i> I can see counting as an Elder Upgrade Power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or not really? A Celerity devotion, which when used reduces the cast time of the next power to be cast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T06:30:59-07:00","id":847650,"title":"","content":"I dunno, that doesn't sound quite right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T06:33:33-07:00","id":847652,"title":"","content":"Well at this point it's a matter of preference. A higher lvl Celerity devotion, or a combines low celerity + another power devotion to speed up that single power? both seem viable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:50:11-07:00","id":847684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847296#post847296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Borrowing a couple of template abilities doesn't mean I'm making vampire into mage.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, it just means that you're not developing things with an eye towards Vampire games. You're just nailing on random power boosts. And that is undesirable from a game design standpoint. Simply slapping on powers simply because someone else did it is lazy. I'm sorry, but it is. You have several things that are inconsistant with the themes and lore of Vampire as it is, and doesn't create stories or leave open plot hooks to work with.<br /> <br /> As for the whole Celeritous thing? You missed the point. Your entire thing started off with a &quot;I can't believe that Devotions are the only thing elders get!&quot; stance, and then, you go and create things that effectively devotions? All you have is renamed Devotions. You didn't create anything new here at all.<br /> <br /> I'm out. See ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:55:10-07:00","id":847685,"title":"","content":"Well, even if they are relatively reproducible with devotions, most are either going to be a series of devotions, or extremely costly ones. Your making a mistake on the relative costs associated. With the transmutations as new innate aspects, they have the capability to be inherently less costly, or inherent. Vitae costs per month and things? No, I'll take innate aspects any day.<br /> <br /> And in that case, why have bloodline gifts or bloodlines? That could just be devotions too right (and is in many cases). Why have sorcery? Most sorcery effects could probably be reproduced with devotions also!<br /> <br /> See that sounds a bit absurd when you start thinking about it. Devotions could do everything these others do also, but they are still options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 03-15-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:48:13-07:00","id":847740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847241#post847241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmrrrr...... *glances through* Well, not bad, but one thing springs instantly to mind. I honestly think you're trying to equate vampire elders to archmages or Gentry here. Elders are equivalent to Master mages or the royalty of Changeling Courts. The Methusalah, vampires who surpass elders, are the ones who adapt new templates like Archmages and True Fae. Of course you'll be disappointed if you think that elder devotions are supposed to be the equivalent of archmastery. They're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall the elder section in 2e saying something about a chrysalis, if you can hold on to your Requiem long enough. I get what you're saying, should a Methuselah just be an aging thing? Is it a deeper transformation that removes vampires from the cycle of redeath (neonate to ancilla to elder to recently awakened BP1 vampire)? The term blood god has also been thrown around a lot, but that too feels too simplistic. It doesn't consider what vampires are in Chronicles of Darkness on a deeper level.<br /> <br /> Don't know if it's relevant, or helpful, but here's a piece of in-game notes by my LARP vampire character, on Vampirism and how it relates to his Requiem as a Theban Sorcerer.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, I can believe that Longinus pierced the Christ's sides, and was damned by a single taste of the Messiah's blood. But these folks did not once stop and ask why that happened. Let's say Jesus was who theologians say He was. That makes him the archetype of Humanity, a perfect representation of what we could be, should be, ought to be. Now look around, does it seem like that kind of person could come out of something as fucked up as human society? Didn't think so. So he was a manifestation of divinity, an emanation in its pure form, here and now. The school of Kabbalah calls that an emanation of a Sephirot, and it's nothing new. Christ was Man (and Woman) in that he manifested our perfect image from Plato's World of Forms. Christ was also God, in that any Sephirot contains within it divine energy, and since Man and Woman were made in His image, the Christ represented the Partzufim, the visage of Divinity into Humanity (and reminded us of what was lost when we foolishly decided to exist as individuals and forsook our collective consciousness, but that's another story).<br /> So there was Longinus, faced with mystical energy at work far beyond the grasp of the average Roman soldier. And what does he do? Apparently, turn into a five-year-old child and poke at it with a pointy stick to see if it's dead\u2026 I know, I know. At that moment, he became a Vampire (though definitely not <i>the</i> Vampire). That's a simple matter of cause-and-effect. What happens to a human when she loses any possible connection with her higher self? What kind of human doesn't have a representation outside the material, having severed his connection to the world of forms? </div> </div> </div>Everyone says how Vampires are creatures of the material (despite the Strix and their role in early Kindred history). Perhaps Kindred are a twisted, Qliphothic representation of the human form. Perhaps, through Ahra, that deformation can be refined and perfected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 03-15-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T11:52:25-07:00","id":847781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847599#post847599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regeneration, page 198. Requires protean 4 and resilience 4, so under the new experience system is would even cost 4 experiences,making it completely identical to Tireless Regeneration aside from the prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see it now. Amusingly enough, if you'll look back you'll see I added that as an afterthought at someone else's request. But anyway...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847616#post847616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but what's the point of making up a completely new system when the old one can do the job?<br /> <br /> Let's see, going over your document seeing what devotions these could be:<br /> *Snip*<br /> <br /> <br /> Really, when I started this list, I thought it's gonna be hard one. But for the most part, these powers fit in devotions so <b>neatly, </b>that I was quite surprised.<br /> So anyways, this does not work a little differently. It's just superficial differences at most, as we get to call these Devotions a different name with a little different pricing scheme.<br /> <br /> And that can be achieved much more easily, by providing a small &quot;elder&quot; template, which allows an Elder to use some Devotions much more cheaply than their counterparts can, giving all and more to the possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I disagree with the ease that you say some of those would be ported to using a devotion with the listed disciplines. Sure, some might work, to an extent, but the actual mechanics would likely be a lot different in some cases.<br /> <br /> Which goes to the second point that Rani already covered. Just because you might be able to make it work with an existing system doesn't mean that's the best way to do it. I mean, for instance, Coil of the Ascendant, Surmounting the Daysleep? Maybe combine Auspex with Protean or even Resilience to function during the day. The Warm Face? Resilience alone, to make something work longer, as you've implied for some of my Transmutations. Could do the same with some Blood Sorcery; Cheval is an Auspex devotion, easily, the Hydra's Vitae screams Protean, etc etc.<br /> <br /> The point being is that these have a different thematic with different limitations. It's not a combination of disciplines, it's a change to how the Kindred functions, and I feel a lot of the Transmutations I provided work best that way. Sure, I will admit a few would fit neatly as devotions (not as many as you say do), but that doesn't mean that's the only or better way for it to work.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and to note, I know elders aren't static creatures anymore, that was more a 'mainstream' sort of view I was pulling from; most modern media paints elders as out of touch and unwilling to change, even if that's not the case for vampires. The transmutation was really just a way of confirming that it is indeed not the case. I'll tweak the wording slightly, though, make that clearer)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=847684#post847684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, it just means that you're not developing things with an eye towards Vampire games. You're just nailing on random power boosts. And that is undesirable from a game design standpoint. Simply slapping on powers simply because someone else did it is lazy. I'm sorry, but it is. You have several things that are inconsistant with the themes and lore of Vampire as it is, and doesn't create stories or leave open plot hooks to work with.<br /> <br /> As for the whole Celeritous thing? You missed the point. Your entire thing started off with a &quot;I can't believe that Devotions are the only thing elders get!&quot; stance, and then, you go and create things that effectively devotions? All you have is renamed Devotions. You didn't create anything new here at all.<br /> <br /> I'm out. See ya.</div> </div> </div> </div>You yourself seem to be getting almost offended by a bit of homebrew, based on your tone there. I'll just simply say I obviously disagree with what you said here (In its entirety), and you obviously have a different view on Vampire's themes than me, and not go into further depth, since you're tapping out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-15-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T18:22:41-07:00","id":849059,"title":"","content":"I really like the concept of ancient vampires transforming into something more than they were -- especially if they can maintain their sanity throughout their immortality. I'll likely crib from your work for my setting. I have one vampire active in the setting who is truly ancient, so she'll definitely have some of these enhancements. Haven't decided if those who are newly Potency 6 will be getting the transmutations -- it may vary by individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:32:04-07:00","id":849429,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\">falco1029</a></b> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\">What is your take on the unholey then?</a></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:30:32-07:00","id":849455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=849429#post849429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\">falco1029</a></b> <b>What is your take on the unholey then?</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This I would like to see also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:52:17-07:00","id":849468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders?p=849059#post849059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the concept of ancient vampires transforming into something more than they were -- especially if they can maintain their sanity throughout their immortality. I'll likely crib from your work for my setting. I have one vampire active in the setting who is truly ancient, so she'll definitely have some of these enhancements. Haven't decided if those who are newly Potency 6 will be getting the transmutations -- it may vary by individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! And yeah, it doesn't have to be something that's immediately available or anything, makes sense some might need to spend some time at that potency to truly transform.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Unholy, you two mean the sort of mechanics/sheet I'd apply to her? Or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:48:19-07:00","id":849542,"title":"","content":"I would love to see your write-up/sheet of her (Immortal Sinners probably best resource) if you have any ideas there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T19:46:40-07:00","id":849578,"title":"","content":"Well, rather than the Devotion she has in Night Horrors, she likely has an Elder Devotion (I'm not against having them, remember, just against that being the only option) that allows Animalism 5 to be used to create a 'portable' territory that automatically follows her but otherwise works like Lord of the Land (it suits the motiff of her not giving care to the domains of others; wherever she goes, it's HER domain). It'd also provide a benefit that any animal within that area that eats kindred flesh or drinks their blood conveys the corresponding amount of Vitae to her.<br /> <br /> Her swarms of birds could likely be done simply using Summon the Hunt now, so it doesn't need its own special thing, but she likely has Immutable Power or similar to more easily keep a swarm or so nearby at all times (A command like 'protect me' or the like imbued permanently into them). That'd also allow her to have Protean 4 active permanently, when she wants to, among other things.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'd probably give her a unique Transmutation of her own, maybe building off of the Unholy being a reminder of what Kindred can eventually become (for good or ill). Perhaps a Transmutation that effectively raises her Blood Potency for positive things only when in the presence of other Kindred?<br /> <br /> As a note, I also want to do something utilizing what I see as an implied connection to Beast's Dark Mother (&quot;Mother of Monsters&quot;, etc), but am not sure what, considering what's shown of her implies she doesn't do much regarding crossover, so I'm a little stuck there. Maybe just a sidenote that she's temporarily made into the Apex of whatever Hive she's closest to and that her 'territory' touches on, on the Beast side. Doesn't affect Vampire games, but would make her an interesting storyhook for Beasts too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if that sounds cool, I could attempt to put together an actual sheet for you guys, if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-19-2016, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}